Phloem Mortis
Ingredients: GOTHIC ROCK & DEATHROCK + BEBOP + COZY, WARM & CHILL LO-FI + Brass
Creative Catalyst: Renegade ethnobotanists attached galvanic micro-electrodes to carnivorous canopy flora, transmuting botanical action potentials into hyperactive bebop brass cadenzas and tape-saturated deathrock dirges.

Phloem Mortis sounds like an unholy velvet cabaret staged inside an overgrown Victorian conservatory at 3:00 AM. Driving tribal tom-toms and ice-cold, flanged chorus basslines lock against frantic, lightning-fast bebop trumpet alterations, all cradled in the soothing, dusty crackle of warbling cassette tape hiss and warm flugelhorn pads. It is simultaneously venomous and slumberous: theatrical batcave theatrics collide head-on with Dizzy Gillespie-level chromatic runs, sweetened by the warm fireside glow of downtempo lo-fi bedroom production and the eerie hum of photosynthetic bio-electricity.

Genre DNA
* Tempo & Pulse: 135–165 BPM; polyrhythmic tension pitting a rigid, hard-driving post-punk deathrock bass-and-snare pummel against slippery, swung bebop brass phrasing and lazy, un-quantized SP-404 lo-fi micro-swings.
* Harmonic Palette: Dark Phrygian dominant and Dorian modes crashing into altered bebop dominant scales (b9, #9, #11); plush minor-ninth chords instantly poisoned by jagged, flatted-fifth brass stabs.
 Production Signatures: Phytogalvanic Sidechaining (compressors triggered dynamically by electrical spikes from living ficus leaves); Cassette-Bake Saturation (horn sections run through degraded Type-I magnetic cassettes soaked in dehumidifier runoff); Crypt-Plate Ambience* (cavernous, metallic goth-rock reverbs abruptly gated behind intimate, lo-fi vinyl hiss).
* Dynamics: Tracks typically open in deceptive, cozy intimacy—crackling needle drops and muted, velvet brass—before rupturing into manic, high-velocity deathrock bass runs and dizzying brass solos, only to collapse without warning back into sleepy, rain-soaked greenhouse hums.

